 "method": {
  "strips": "land within 0-200 m and 200-500 m of the Oct 2024 shoreline (Phase 11 baseline), the sea (Phase 11 sea polygons) removed; rasters at 10 m, areas are sums of pixel areas; a pixel 200 m away is in the inner strip",
  "built": "Dynamic World V1 `built` (label 6): the per-pixel mode of the label over the month / dry season (monthly.class_image)",
  "gaps": "a strip-month with Dynamic World on under 50% of its land is a gap (built_ha null): the monsoon months, not zeros",
  "seasons": "dry-season (Oct-Mar) modes (monthly.dry_seasons); change over the pixels observed in both seasons",
  "patches": "built in the last dry season, not in the first, observed in both; >= 0.5 ha connected (8-neighbour); split where they cross the 200 m line; area_ha computed from the polygon",
  "open_buildings": "GOOGLE/Research/open-buildings-temporal/v1 `building_presence` yearly mosaic, area where the confidence >= [0.3, 0.5, 0.7] (headline 0.5) at 4 m; uncalibrated confidence, footprints only (Dynamic World also counts roads, ports, yards): reference only, not part of the evaluation",
  "units": "hectares of built area, never building counts (10 m, D11)",
  "caveats": "Dynamic World labels bare ground, coal yards and port apron as built in places and the mode flickers between built / bare from month to month: trust the dry-season figures and the trend over the single months; the strips follow the 2024 coast, so for earlier windows the strip is where the coast is now"
 }
